# Copy this file to .env and fill in every value below — ALL of them are
# required. This app has no local file storage: every branch/owner
# credential and every piece of business data (employees, drivers, tip
# entries, delivery entries) lives in a Google Sheet — but WHICH Sheet is the
# owner's own choice, made from the dashboard after deploying (Settings >
# connect a Google Sheet), not something you set here.
#
# What you DO set here is a small "control" Sheet (GOOGLE_SHEET_ID below)
# that this app uses internally to remember which Sheet the owner picked —
# it never holds any business data itself. Any blank Google Sheet works; you
# never need to open it or set anything up inside it.
#
# ---- One-time setup in https://console.cloud.google.com/ ----
#   1. Create a project (or pick an existing one).
#   2. Enable the "Google Sheets API" and the "Google Drive API" (APIs &
#      Services -> Library -> search for each -> Enable). Drive is needed
#      only for the moment an owner clicks "Create a new Sheet for me".
#   3. "Configure consent screen" -> External -> fill the required fields
#      (app name, your email) -> Save. Testing mode is fine for personal use.
#   4. On the consent screen's "Data Access" page, add the sensitive scopes
#      ".../auth/spreadsheets" and ".../auth/drive.file".
#   5. On the consent screen's "Audience" page, add every Gmail address that
#      will ever click "Sign in with Google" or "Connect a Google Sheet"
#      under "Test users" — required for an unverified Testing-mode app to
#      grant a sensitive scope to that account. This includes the owner's
#      own Gmail address.
#   6. "Create Credentials" -> "OAuth client ID" -> Application type: Web
#      application. Under "Authorized redirect URIs", add BOTH
#      GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI and GOOGLE_SHEETS_REDIRECT_URI below (the
#      http://localhost:3000/... ones for local dev; your production URL +
#      the same two paths for a real deployment). Copy the generated Client
#      ID and Client Secret.
#   7. Get a refresh token once, for the CONTROL Sheet only: temporarily run
#      the app locally, and use Google's OAuth Playground
#      (https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground) with your own Client
#      ID/Secret and the scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets
#      to mint one directly. This is a one-time step for whoever deploys the
#      app — it has nothing to do with the owner's own Sheet connection,
#      which owners set up themselves through the app, not this file.
#   8. Create a blank Google Sheet (any name) to act as the control Sheet,
#      and copy its ID from the URL:
#      https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/THIS_PART_IS_THE_ID/edit

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_SHEETS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/google-sheets/callback

# The control Sheet (see step 8 above) — NOT the owner's business-data
# Sheet, which is connected later from the dashboard itself.
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=

# Required, and must be a FIXED value (not left blank) as soon as more than
# one server process might handle requests — e.g. on Vercel, where a login
# on one serverless instance must still be recognized by a different
# instance handling the next request. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
SESSION_SECRET=
